// no-server-key: read-only — pending Stage A-E member-signed-writes refactor per ADR-2605231525
//
// cljs migration note (svelte-to-cljs wave 10): this repo differs from most
// sibling migrations. `main` was ALREADY `src/app.ts` before this change —
// it never pointed at a SvelteKit build output, so this migration leaves it
// untouched; that path is not this migration's business.
//
// The only thing this migration touches here is `assets.directory`, which
// pointed at the now-deleted `./svelte/build` (the retired SvelteKit
// frontend's build output) and now points at `./cljs/public` (the new
// shadow-cljs + reagent + re-frame + jp-go-dds static bundle, see cljs/).
//
// Flagged, not fixed, by this migration: `src/app.ts` (this Worker's
// `main`) does not reference `ASSETS` or call `env.ASSETS.fetch(...)`
// anywhere in its handler (verified by reading the file and grepping it for
// both identifiers — zero matches). That means the asset bundle this
// `assets.directory` points at is not reachable through this Worker's own
// fetch handler; Cloudflare's own assets routing may still serve it ahead
// of the Worker depending on deployment configuration, but this migration
// does not verify that either way. This is a PRE-EXISTING condition (the
// same was true when `assets.directory` pointed at `./svelte/build`) — not
// something introduced or something this migration attempts to fix.
//
// `vars.APP_FRAMEWORK` is `"ts-native"`, not a `sveltekit-*` value, so it is
// left unchanged.
//
// This edit is UNVERIFIED: `wrangler deploy` / `wrangler dev` were NOT run
// against it.
